EXT. BOCCE COURT UNDER HIGHWAY OVERPASS - DAY

A strip of crushed oyster shell beneath concrete pillars. Traffic thunders overhead. Folding chairs line the court. A thermos of espresso sits on an overturned crate.

NONNA FILOMENA, eighties, in a black dress and sensible shoes, squints at the pallino. BIG WALT, fifties, her opponent, a trucker in a leather vest, crouches with a ball cradled in his palm. DARIUS, fifteen, Walt's nephew, holds the measuring string and a notebook.

She straightens, shifts her weight, and sends her ball down the shell with a sharp flick of the wrist while he lobs his in a high arc, and the two collide mid-court in a crack that scatters dust, and the pallino rolls under a chair where Darius scrambles after it on his knees.

NONNA FILOMENA
That's mine.

BIG WALT
That's a tie.

DARIUS
It's closer to the chair.

NONNA FILOMENA
Darius, measure!

BIG WALT
Don't measure, Darius.

DARIUS
I'm measuring.

NONNA FILOMENA
Walt, you cheat.

BIG WALT
Nonna, I've never cheated in my life.

DARIUS
It's four inches.

NONNA FILOMENA
Four inches for who?

BIG WALT
For me, obviously.

DARIUS
For her.

Walt looks at Darius. Darius looks at Nonna. She lifts the thermos, takes one sip, and offers it to Walt.
